    "answer": {
      "short": "$(2,5)$ and $(5,26)$.",
      "worked": "Equate the expressions for $y$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+1&=7x-9\\\\x^2-7x+10&=0\\\\(x-2)(x-5)&=0\\\\x&=2\\text{ or }x=5\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x=2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=7(2)-9\\\\y&=5\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x=5$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=7(5)-9\\\\y&=26\\end{align*}$$\nThe intersection points are $(2,5)$ and $(5,26)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
